{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"I fixed the stuck cleanup and submitted the mitigation. The submission endpoint returned 200. I haven't seen the validation result yet.\n\nThe cause was a `ConfigMap` called `reservation-cleanup-token`, stuck in `Terminating`. A finalizer held it, and the `cleanup-controller` that should remove that finalizer was getting HTTP 403 on every attempt. Its `ClusterRole`, `configmap-cleanup-controller`, only allowed `get`, `list` and `watch` on `ConfigMap`s.\n\nI added `patch` and `update` to that role. The controller then cleared the finalizer and the `ConfigMap` was deleted.\n\nI didn't find any other fault. The application pods were all `Running`, and `profile` and `search` each had one restart right after startup. I did not send any test requests to the application, so I haven't confirmed end-user requests succeed."}}
